!!! Serving a directory of files.
!!!
!!! The whole job is one decision made correctly — which bytes on disk a URL
!!! path is allowed to name — and the ways that decision goes wrong are well
!!! known enough to enumerate. Each check below is one of them.
!!!
!!! The file is read whole into text. That is fine for the stylesheets and
!!! scripts a page needs and wrong for anything large, and it is what the
!!! runtime offers: `file.read_text` reads a whole file, and the streaming
!!! handles exist but there is nothing to stream *to* until there is a socket.
!!! `maximum-bytes` keeps a large file from being read at all rather than
!!! pretending it can be served.

book nilweb.static.files

read nil.std.io.file
read nil.std.core
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read nil.std.text
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.status
read everything from nilweb.http.headers
read everything from nilweb.http.request
read everything from nilweb.http.method
read everything from nilweb.crypto.sha256
read everything from nilweb.time.clock
read everything from nilweb.http.response


!!! Larger than this and the answer is 413 rather than a read that would hold
!!! the whole thing in memory to hand to a transport that must then hold it
!!! again. Two megabytes covers a web font; a video is not this module's job.
constant maximum-bytes as number is 2097152


!!! --- Serve `path` from under `root`.
!!!
!!! The response is complete, including its Content-Type, or it is the right
!!! refusal. A 404 is given for anything the caller may not have, including
!!! things that exist — a probe must not be able to tell a file it may not see
!!! from a file that is not there.

public serve-file receives root as text, path as text returns http-response begin paragraph
    value relative is without-leading-slash with path being path
    when not (is-safe-name with name being relative) then
        give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
    end when
    when relative equals "" then
        give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
    end when

    value full is when root equals "" give relative otherwise give root plus "/" plus relative end when
    when not (nil.std.io::exists with path being full) then
        give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
    end when

    value measured is nil.std.io::size with path being full
    consider measured
        !!! `begin block` because this arm holds its own `when`: without it
        !!! the nested conditional reads as the next pattern arm.
        when Result.Ok holding width then begin block
            when width is greater than maximum-bytes then
                give error-response with code being status-payload-too-large,
                    explanation being "That file is too large to serve"
            end when
        end block
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
        otherwise
            give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
    end consider

    value outcome is nil.std.io::read_text with path being full
    consider outcome
        when Result.Ok holding body then
            give make-response with code being status-ok,
                kind being (media-type-of with name being relative), body being body
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
        otherwise
            give error-response with code being status-not-found, explanation being "No such file"
    end consider
end paragraph


!!! --- Serve a file and ask the client to keep it.
!!! Only for assets whose name changes when their content does; a cached
!!! `/style.css` is how a deploy ships to half its users.

public serve-cached receives root as text, path as text, seconds as number returns http-response begin paragraph
    value answer is serve-file with root being root, path being path
    when answer.code does not equal status-ok then
        give answer
    end when
    give with-header with response being answer, name being "Cache-Control",
        content being "public, max-age=" plus (seconds becomes text)
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether a path from a URL may name a file.
!!!
!!! Refused by shape rather than resolved and then checked. Resolving first
!!! means trusting whatever the platform does with the name, and the platform
!!! that does something unexpected is always the one not tested. Every refusal
!!! here costs a legitimate file nothing, because none of these shapes appear
!!! in a name anyone meant to publish.

public is-safe-name receives name as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    !!! Climbing out, in any spelling the path layer might later collapse.
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being ".." then give false end when
    !!! Absolute, or a Windows drive or UNC name.
    when nil.std.text::starts_with with s being name, prefix being "/" then give false end when
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being ":" then give false end when
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being "\" then give false end when
    !!! A null byte truncates the name for whatever C function sees it last.
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being (zero-byte with nothing) then give false end when
    !!! A dotfile is configuration, not content: .env, .git, .htpasswd.
    when nil.std.text::starts_with with s being name, prefix being "." then give false end when
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being "/." then give false end when
    !!! An empty segment means a doubled separator, which some path layers
    !!! collapse and some do not. Not worth finding out which this one is.
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being "//" then give false end when
    give true
end paragraph


zero-byte returns text begin paragraph
    give nil.std.core::Convert.i32_to_char with code being 0
end paragraph


without-leading-slash receives path as text returns text begin paragraph
    variable out as text is path
    repeat while nil.std.text::starts_with with s being out, prefix being "/"
        set out to nil.std.text::substring with s being out, start being 1,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being out) minus 1
    end repeat
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- The media type for a name, by its last suffix.
!!!
!!! An unknown suffix is application/octet-stream and never text/html. A
!!! browser told something is HTML will run the script in it, so guessing
!!! generously here is how an upload directory becomes a cross-site scripting
!!! hole. `charset=utf-8` is stated for every text type, because a browser
!!! left to guess an encoding guesses, and sometimes picks one that turns a
!!! harmless file into markup.

public media-type-of receives name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value folded is nil.std.text::to_lower with s being name
    value suffix is last-extension with name being folded
    give switch suffix
        case "html" then stop switching with "text/html; charset=utf-8"
        case "htm" then stop switching with "text/html; charset=utf-8"
        case "css" then stop switching with "text/css; charset=utf-8"
        case "js" then stop switching with "text/javascript; charset=utf-8"
        case "mjs" then stop switching with "text/javascript; charset=utf-8"
        case "json" then stop switching with "application/json"
        case "txt" then stop switching with "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
        case "md" then stop switching with "text/markdown; charset=utf-8"
        case "csv" then stop switching with "text/csv; charset=utf-8"
        case "xml" then stop switching with "application/xml"
        case "svg" then stop switching with "image/svg+xml"
        case "png" then stop switching with "image/png"
        case "jpg" then stop switching with "image/jpeg"
        case "jpeg" then stop switching with "image/jpeg"
        case "gif" then stop switching with "image/gif"
        case "webp" then stop switching with "image/webp"
        case "avif" then stop switching with "image/avif"
        case "ico" then stop switching with "image/x-icon"
        case "woff" then stop switching with "font/woff"
        case "woff2" then stop switching with "font/woff2"
        case "ttf" then stop switching with "font/ttf"
        case "otf" then stop switching with "font/otf"
        case "pdf" then stop switching with "application/pdf"
        case "wasm" then stop switching with "application/wasm"
        otherwise stop switching with "application/octet-stream"
    end switch
end paragraph


last-extension receives name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value dot is nil.std.text::last_index_of with s being name, needle being "."
    when dot is less than 0 then
        give ""
    end when
    value slash is nil.std.text::last_index_of with s being name, needle being "/"
    when dot is less than slash then
        give ""
    end when
    value after is dot plus 1
    give nil.std.text::substring with s being name, start being after,
        length being (nil.std.text::length with s being name) minus after
end paragraph


!!! =============================================================================
!!! Revalidation, ranges, and a content cache
!!! =============================================================================
!!!
!!! `serve-file` above answers every request with the whole file, which is
!!! correct and wasteful: a browser that already has the stylesheet fetches it
!!! again on every page, and a client resuming a download starts over. These
!!! are the three things a static file server is expected to do about that.


!!! --- A file's identity, for deciding whether a client's copy is current.

public validators begin record
    field found as boolean
    field width as number
    field stamped-at as number
    field tag as text
end record


!!! --- Identity of the bytes actually served.
!!!
!!! Hashing the representation prevents equal-length edits with preserved
!!! timestamps from reusing an ETag. A request reads content once and hashes
!!! that same body; Last-Modified is supplemental, second-resolution metadata.

public validators-of receives root as text, path as text returns validators begin paragraph
    value answer is serve-file with root being root, path being path
    when answer.code does not equal status-ok then
        give build validators with found being false, width being 0, stamped-at being 0, tag being ""
    end when
    give validators-for-body with root being root, path being path, body being answer.body
end paragraph


validators-for-body receives root as text, path as text, body as text returns validators begin paragraph
    value relative is without-leading-slash with path being path
    value full is when root equals "" give relative otherwise give root plus "/" plus relative end when
    variable stamped as number is 0 minus 1
    value timed is nil.std.io::modified_at with path being full
    consider timed
        when Result.Ok holding at-ms then set stamped to at-ms
        otherwise set stamped to 0 minus 1
    end consider
    give build validators with found being true,
        width being (nil.std.text::length with s being body), stamped-at being stamped,
        tag being quote plus (sha256-hex with data being body) plus quote
end paragraph


!!! --- Ordinary failures precede conditions; conditions precede Range.
!!! RFC 9110 sections 13.2.1 and 13.2.2. A present empty tag field still
!!! suppresses its date fallback. If-Match compares strongly; If-None-Match
!!! compares weakly and returns 304 only for GET/HEAD, otherwise 412.

public serve-revalidated receives root as text, path as text, request as http-request,
    seconds as number returns http-response begin paragraph
    value answer is serve-file with root being root, path being path
    when answer.code does not equal status-ok then give answer end when
    value marks is validators-for-body with root being root, path being path, body being answer.body
    value full is with-validators with response being answer, marks being marks, seconds being seconds
    when (method-name with verb being request.verb) equals "OPTIONS" then give full end when

    value has-match is has-field with fields being request.fields, name being "If-Match"
    when has-match then
        when not (tag-matches with offered being (list-field with fields being request.fields,
            name being "If-Match"), tag being marks.tag, strong being true) then
            give precondition-failed with nothing
        end when
    otherwise
        value unmodified is valid-date with stated being (single-field with fields being request.fields,
            name being "If-Unmodified-Since")
        when marks.stamped-at is at least 0 and unmodified is at least 0
            and (marks.stamped-at over 1000) is greater than (unmodified over 1000) then
            give precondition-failed with nothing
        end when
    end when

    value retrieval is (method-name with verb being request.verb) equals "GET" or (method-name with verb being request.verb) equals "HEAD"
    value has-none-match is has-field with fields being request.fields, name being "If-None-Match"
    when has-none-match then
        when tag-matches with offered being (list-field with fields being request.fields,
            name being "If-None-Match"), tag being marks.tag, strong being false then
            when retrieval then
                give with-validators with response being (empty-response with code being status-not-modified),
                    marks being marks, seconds being seconds
            end when
            give precondition-failed with nothing
        end when
    end when
    when not has-none-match and retrieval and (not-modified-since with stated being (single-field with fields being request.fields,
        name being "If-Modified-Since"), stamped-at being marks.stamped-at) then
        give with-validators with response being (empty-response with code being status-not-modified),
            marks being marks, seconds being seconds
    end when
    give full
end paragraph


with-validators receives response as http-response, marks as validators,
    seconds as number returns http-response begin paragraph
    variable answer is with-header with response being response, name being "ETag", content being marks.tag
    when marks.stamped-at is at least 0 then
        set answer to with-header with response being answer, name being "Last-Modified",
            content being (http-date with at-ms being marks.stamped-at)
    end when
    give with-header with response being answer, name being "Cache-Control",
        content being "public, max-age=" plus (seconds becomes text)
end paragraph


precondition-failed returns http-response begin paragraph
    give error-response with code being status-precondition-failed, explanation being "The file does not meet the request conditions"
end paragraph


!!! The current clock reader supports IMF-fixdate. Canonical round-tripping
!!! rejects malformed separators, impossible calendar dates and wrong weekdays.
!!! Unrecognised dates, including obsolete HTTP-date spellings, are ignored.

valid-date receives stated as text returns number begin paragraph
    value trimmed is nil.std.text::trim with s being stated
    value parsed is ms-from-http-date with stated being trimmed
    when parsed is less than 0 then give 0 minus 1 end when
    when (http-date with at-ms being parsed) does not equal trimmed then give 0 minus 1 end when
    give parsed
end paragraph


not-modified-since receives stated as text, stamped-at as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    value held is valid-date with stated being stated
    when held is less than 0 or stamped-at is less than 0 then give false end when
    give (stamped-at over 1000) is at most (held over 1000)
end paragraph


!!! List fields may be repeated; singleton date/If-Range fields may not.

list-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value held is field-values with fields being fields, name being name
    variable joined as text is ""
    variable first as boolean is true
    repeat for each one in held
        when not first then set joined to joined plus "," end when
        set joined to joined plus one
        set first to false
    end repeat
    give joined
end paragraph


single-field receives fields as array of header-field, name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value held is field-values with fields being fields, name being name
    when the length of held does not equal 1 then give "" end when
    give held at 0
end paragraph


!!! Parse entity-tag lists without splitting commas inside opaque quoted tags.
!!! Validate the whole list before accepting a match, and only permit the weak
!!! prefix for weak comparison. Backslashes have no escape meaning in an ETag.

tag-matches receives offered as text, tag as text, strong as boolean returns boolean begin paragraph
    value input is nil.std.text::trim with s being offered
    when input equals "*" then give true end when
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being input
    variable index as number is 0
    variable matched as boolean is false
    repeat while index is less than width
        variable code as number is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being input, index being index
        when code equals 32 or code equals 9 or code equals 44 then
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise
            variable weak as boolean is false
            when (nil.std.text::substring with s being input, start being index, length being 2) equals "W/" then
                set weak to true
                set index to index plus 2
            end when
            when index is at least width then give false end when
            when (nil.std.text::byte_at with s being input, index being index) does not equal 34 then give false end when
            value first is index
            set index to index plus 1
            variable closed as boolean is false
            repeat while index is less than width and not closed
                set code to nil.std.text::byte_at with s being input, index being index
                when code equals 34 then
                    set closed to true
                end when
                when code is less than 33 or code equals 127 then give false end when
                set index to index plus 1
            end repeat
            when not closed then give false end when
            value bare is nil.std.text::substring with s being input, start being first, length being index minus first
            when bare equals tag and (not strong or not weak) then set matched to true end when
            repeat while index is less than width
                set code to nil.std.text::byte_at with s being input, index being index
                when code does not equal 32 and code does not equal 9 then stop repeating end when
                set index to index plus 1
            end repeat
            when index is less than width then
                when (nil.std.text::byte_at with s being input, index being index) does not equal 44 then give false end when
            end when
        end when
    end repeat
    give matched
end paragraph


!!! --- A requested byte range, as the client asked for it.

public asked-range begin record
    field present as boolean
    field satisfiable as boolean
    field first-byte as number
    field last-byte as number
end record


!!! --- Read a Range header against a known length.
!!!
!!! One range only. A multi-range request is answered with the whole file,
!!! which RFC 9110 explicitly permits and which avoids generating a multipart
!!! body for a case almost nothing sends.
!!!
!!! `bytes=-500` means the last 500 bytes, `bytes=500-` means from 500 to the
!!! end, and `bytes=0-0` is the first byte. A first byte past the end is
!!! unsatisfiable and must be answered 416 rather than clamped, because a
!!! client resuming a download that has since shrunk needs to be told.

public range-of receives stated as text, width as number returns asked-range begin paragraph
    value absent is build asked-range with present being false, satisfiable being false,
        first-byte being 0, last-byte being 0
    when stated equals "" or width is at most 0 then
        !!! RFC 9110 permits ignoring Range for an empty representation.
        give absent
    end when
    value trimmed is nil.std.text::trim with s being stated
    when not (nil.std.text::starts_with with s being (nil.std.text::to_lower with s being trimmed), prefix being "bytes=") then
        !!! An unknown unit is ignored, as RFC 9110 requires, rather than
        !!! refused: the whole representation is a valid answer to it.
        give absent
    end when
    value spec is nil.std.text::trim with s being
        (nil.std.text::substring with s being trimmed, start being 6,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being trimmed) minus 6)
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being spec, needle being "," then
        give absent
    end when

    value first-text is before-first with input being spec, separator being "-"
    value last-text is after-first with input being spec, separator being "-"
    when not (nil.std.text::contains with s being spec, needle being "-") then
        give unsatisfiable with nothing
    end when

    !!! A suffix range: the last N bytes.
    when first-text equals "" then
        value wanted is count-of with digits being last-text
        when wanted is at most 0 then
            give unsatisfiable with nothing
        end when
        value taken is when wanted is greater than width give width otherwise give wanted end when
        give build asked-range with present being true, satisfiable being true,
            first-byte being width minus taken, last-byte being width minus 1
    end when

    value first-byte is count-of with digits being first-text
    when first-byte is less than 0 or first-byte is at least width then
        give unsatisfiable with nothing
    end when
    when last-text equals "" then
        give build asked-range with present being true, satisfiable being true,
            first-byte being first-byte, last-byte being width minus 1
    end when
    value last-byte is count-of with digits being last-text
    when last-byte is less than first-byte then
        give unsatisfiable with nothing
    end when
    value clamped is when last-byte is at least width give width minus 1 otherwise give last-byte end when
    give build asked-range with present being true, satisfiable being true,
        first-byte being first-byte, last-byte being clamped
end paragraph


unsatisfiable returns asked-range begin paragraph
    give build asked-range with present being true, satisfiable being false,
        first-byte being 0, last-byte being 0
end paragraph


!!! --- A decimal count, or minus one when the text is not one.
!!! Hand-rolled rather than borrowed, because a Range header is attacker-
!!! supplied and a parser that raises on malformed input is a parser that
!!! stops the server.

count-of receives digits as text returns number begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being digits
    when width is less than 1 then
        give 0 minus 1
    end when
    variable total as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        value code is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being digits, index being index
        when code is less than 48 or code is greater than 57 then
            give 0 minus 1
        end when
        !!! Saturate while continuing to validate every digit. A huge suffix
        !!! or end offset is valid and clamps; a huge first offset cannot fit.
        when total is greater than 922337203685477580
            or (total equals 922337203685477580 and code is greater than 55) then
            set total to 9223372036854775807
        otherwise
            set total to (total times 10) plus (code minus 48)
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


!!! --- Apply ranges only to a GET whose ordinary response would be 200.
!!! HEAD keeps the full body internally so render-response can calculate the
!!! GET Content-Length while suppressing its wire body. If-Range compares a
!!! single strong content ETag. Date validators are not known strong for files
!!! that can be edited more than once a second, so date-form If-Range falls
!!! back to the whole representation (RFC 9110 Last-Modified comparison and If-Range rules).

public serve-static receives root as text, path as text, request as http-request,
    seconds as number returns http-response begin paragraph
    value answer is serve-revalidated with root being root, path being path,
        request being request, seconds being seconds
    when answer.code does not equal status-ok then give answer end when
    value whole is with-header with response being answer, name being "Accept-Ranges", content being "bytes"
    when (method-name with verb being request.verb) does not equal "GET" then give whole end when

    when has-field with fields being request.fields, name being "If-Range" then
        value offered is nil.std.text::trim with s being (single-field with fields being request.fields, name being "If-Range")
        value tag is field-value with fields being whole.fields, name being "ETag"
        when offered does not equal tag then give whole end when
    end when
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being whole.body
    value wanted is range-of with stated being (single-field with fields being request.fields, name being "Range"),
        width being width
    when not wanted.present then give whole end when
    when not wanted.satisfiable then
        value refusal is error-response with code being status-range-not-satisfiable,
            explanation being "That range is outside the file"
        value ranged is with-header with response being refusal, name being "Content-Range",
            content being "bytes */" plus (width becomes text)
        give with-header with response being ranged, name being "Accept-Ranges", content being "bytes"
    end when

    value taken is nil.std.text::substring with s being whole.body, start being wanted.first-byte,
        length being wanted.last-byte minus wanted.first-byte plus 1
    value partial is with-body with response being (with-status with response being whole,
        code being status-partial-content), body being taken
    give with-header with response being partial, name being "Content-Range",
        content being "bytes " plus (wanted.first-byte becomes text) plus "-"
            plus (wanted.last-byte becomes text) plus "/" plus (width becomes text)
end paragraph
